WEBVTT

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:05.000
this is a synthetic test transcript written for the pipeline self test

00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:11.000
a lot of players set up with the ball far too close to their right hip

00:00:11.000 --> 00:00:17.000
when the ball gets that close the arm folds up and the elbow ends up stuck against the ribs

00:00:17.000 --> 00:00:24.000
the reason is usually that they walk straight at the ball instead of leaving space off to the side

00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:31.000
watch Sam here, his feet stop moving early and he ends up crowded at contact

00:00:31.000 --> 00:00:38.000
now I am going to ask him to stand right on top of the ball on purpose so you can see it

00:00:38.000 --> 00:00:46.000
the feeling should be that the ball is almost uncomfortably far away to your right

00:00:46.000 --> 00:00:54.000
a simple drill put a cone half a step outside your contact point and try to hit the ball outside the cone

00:00:54.000 --> 00:01:02.000
if the ball keeps landing short and you feel crowded you are still too close

00:01:02.000 --> 00:01:10.000
here is Sam doing it well, plenty of space and a long smooth swing
